ces arrow-right--line Resources Bookstore arrow-right--line Community & Alumni Calendar arrow-right--line Faculty & Staff Resources Top Resources Academic & Instructional Calendars arrow-right--line Academic Catalog arrow-right--line Canvas arrow-right--line Email arrow-right--line Faculty & Staff Calendar arrow-right--line Luma arrow-right--line Library arrow-right--line Registrar arrow-right--line WarriorHub arrow-right--line Administration Office of the President arrow-right--line Academic Affairs arrow-right--line Administrative Services arrow-right--line Institutional Research & Effectiveness arrow-right--line Student Affairs arrow-right--line School of Arts, Sciences & Innovation arrow-right--line School of Career & Technical Education arrow-right--line School of Health Professions arrow-right--line Policies and Procedures arrow-right--line Classroom Center for Teaching and Learning arrow-right--line WarriorHub arrow-right--line Using Microsoft Teams arrow-right--line Faculty Resources Awards arrow-right--line Performance Review & Job Description arrow-right--line Petition Committee Process arrow-right--line Sabbatical arrow-right--line Forms Administrative arrow-right--line Grants arrow-right--line Human Resources arrow-right--line Purchasing arrow-right--line Security Office arrow-right--line Other Resources 25 Live Calendar arrow-right--line Classified Staff Organization arrow-right--line Faculty Association arrow-right--line Faculty Senate arrow-right--line Human Resource Services arrow-right--line Intranet arrow-right--line IT Ticket System (on campus only) arrow-right--line Logging into IT Accounts arrow-right--line Professional Staff Organization arrow-right--line Qualtrics arrow-right--line Physical Plant Service Request arrow-right--line Testing Center arrow-right--line WarriorWeb arrow-right--line search-find--solid Search What can we help you find? Search for anything and everything LC State Search search-find--solid Submit Menu Degrees 130+ Degrees and Certificates arrow-right--line Admissions Become a Warrior arrow-right--line Affordability Tuition, Aid, and Scholarships arrow-right--line Student Life Activities, Clubs, and Housing arrow-right--line Athletics Keep up with the Warriors arrow-right--line About Perseverance and Possibility arrow-right--line A-Z Directory Academic Calendar Bookstore Campus Calendar Catalog Coeur d'Alene Center Discrimination & Harassment Emergency Information Faculty & Staff Directory Library Offices & Services Directory Transcripts facebook--solid instagram--solid youtube--solid twitter--solid LC State invites you to Do More through an education experience that emphasizes hands-on learning, small class sizes, faculty excellence, student-faculty interaction, and success after graduation. Apply Now arrow-right--line Visit Campus arrow-right--line Request Info arrow-right--line Explore Degrees arrow-right--line School of Career & Technical Education Hospitality Opportunity Request Form School of Career & Technical Education In this Section open-close-angle Signing Day Explore Our Technical & Industrial Programs Faculty Resources State of Idaho CTE Perkins V Staff Directory Hospitality Opportunity Request Dean's List This form is to be used to request services that transfer into Internship Opportunities/Experiences from the Hospitality Management Program at LC State and its students. All services requested by students for Internship Opportunities/Experiences must directly relate to the program of study and the curriculum being taught. Fill out this form completely for consideration Must include Person In Charge contact information Please review sections I and II below to fully understand the Internship Process and Requirements. I: The Internship Experience exit--solid I: The Internship Experience supports preparing students to assume a management “style” role in the Hospitality, Travel & Tourism Industries. Inserted in said role, students will have the responsibility of working in outlined positions/experiences to connect their curriculum-guided education/training in Hospitality Management to “real” hands-on applications. The Internship Experience provides students with the opportunity to use the skills learned in the classroom and to use them in the industry successfully. It allows students to apply their knowledge on how to assist employees, understand policies and procedures, and use the tools needed to succeed in a real position. Students become integral members of the hospitality industry and will gain hands-on experience in facilities management, the day-to-day operations of the business, and the real-world application of knowledge gained from the hospitality degree program. The intern’s time is split between hands-on work, procurement, and industry-related administrative tasks. II: Internship Experience assessments exit--solid II: Internship Experience assessments are acquired through connections based strongly on Business and Market and Management such as logistical planning, inventor and management controls, financial controls, design/creation, supervision, forecasting and projections, and most other aspects of the business and marketing side of the industry. Allowances will be given in limitation to Hospitality Services (FCS) hours relating to this program in the forms of serving tables/banquets, culinary arts applications only, beverage service, setup and takedown applications, and others. With Hospitality Management being formatted more strongly in Business and Marketing constructs, hours for internships need to be elevated above Hospitality Services to be accepted. (*any questions about how internship hours are to be assessed, please meet with the program director(s)) Multiple internship opportunities are formulated throughout the semester(s) with the intent to diversify a student’s Internship Experience within their certificate or degree journey. *Internship Experiences are finalized before each semester with a lead time of 6-8 months before accepting any Internship Experiences. The diversity of Internship Experiences is designed based on the curriculum being taught during that semester. Standards for students to receive credits for this level of coursework is for Internship Opportunities to have a viable connection to the hospitality industry through the following: exit--solid A job in the industry o This is defined by having a job (paid, unpaid, or other) that is specific to or justifiably connected to (review required by professor) the industry of hospitality, travel, and tourism. Course Description II above applies. A philanthropic endeavor in an industry that produces o This is defined by Internship Experiences related to fundraisers, community events, campus events, tours, and others that are specific to or justifiably connected to (review required by professor) the industry of hospitality, travel, and tourism. Course Description II above applies. Agreed upon connection to the industry by instructor and student o This is defined by any Internship Experience that falls outside of the above two bullet points. A conversation is required with an advisor of the program to justify this possibility. Internship Opportunity Experience Form-Hospitality Management/Culinary Arts Name of your Internship Opportunity Experience you wish to obtain services from Hospitality Management at LC State. * Person In Charge contact information-Include Name, Phone Number(s), email Address(s) * DATE, TIME, and LOCATION, HOURS NEEDED of your Internship Opportunity Experience * Describe your \"EVENT\" and list the needs/services of your Internship Opportunity Experience you wish to obtain from Hospitality Management at LC State. * How do you or your organization feel this Internship Opportunity/Experience pertains to the Hospitality Management Program at LC State? * Non-Profit or For Profit - Please expand * Check the needs/services you are considering for the Internship Opportunity Experience that you wish to obtain from Hospitality Management at LC State. * Service- Students acting in the role of server/busser (Plated, Buffet, Beverage, Passed, other Design- Students acting in the role of designer (Layout, Center Pieces, Table Scape, Décor, Plating Design, other) Culinary- Students acting in the role of Culinary Skills (Chef, Prep Work, Catering Essentials, Menu Items, Action Stations, other) Logistical Planning- Students acting in the role of Planner (Wedding, Life Cycle Coordination, Fundraising, Event Logistics, other) Speaker/Representative-Student acting as a guest speaker or representative in any manner. Other: Is your organization LC State Campus affiliated? * Yes No What is your Campus affiliation-(division, club, department, other) * Will your organization be donating to the Hospitality Management Program at LC State? * Yes No Donation type considered * Monetary In-Kind/Tangible Items Marketing None at this time Donation Link(s) https://www.lcsc.edu/giving Consent for storing submitted data * Yes, I give permission to store and process my data Contact Information contact-card--solid Career & Technical Education Mechanical Technical Building 500 8th Avenue Lewiston, Idaho 83501 calls--solid 208-792-2225 print--solid 208-792-2816 (fax) envelope--solid ctedean@lcsc.edu time--solid Mon-Fri, 8:00 - 5:00 Learn More. Do More. #LCState #TheWarriorWay Join us in helping students Do More. Give to LC State arrow-right--line Academic Calendar Map & Directions Emergency Information Provide Feedback Consumer Information Contact Information Offices & Services Directory facebook--solid instagram--solid youtube--solid twitter--solid pin--solid 500 8th Avenue, Lewiston, Idaho 83501 calls--solid 208-792-5272 Accessibility Public Safety Discrimination & Harassment Privacy Policy Terms of Use © Lewis-Clark State College Chat with us , powered by LiveChat"
    },
